WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
Hi, it's almost time to say goodbye,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.610
but we have a little time left

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.820
for some of your questions.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.260
First up is a Twitter question

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.470
from Camille, she asked,
what has your experience

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.540
on the #DrewBarrymoreShow
taught you so far?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.380
Wow, you would think, you know,

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.120
only having been on the air a week.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.170
I wouldn't know much,

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.870
but we've actually been
in this for many months

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.160
over a year, trying to
get this show launched,

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.060
so I have learned a lot.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.420
And the truth is (claps)

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.970
I think that this show is inspiring me

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.530
to really be the best version of myself

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.570
that I have ever been.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.530
It's what my kids do for me.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.428
But this show, just like
my friends and loved ones

00:00:39.428 --> 00:00:42.150
they all just want to make me--

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.450
they make me want to be a better person.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.700
That's the truth answer.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.360
All right, let's get a question
from our virtual friends,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.619
Crystal, what do you got for me?

00:00:49.619 --> 00:00:50.771
(gaps)

00:00:50.771 --> 00:00:52.227
- Hi Drew, how are you?

00:00:52.227 --> 00:00:54.618
- Oh, I am loving your look.

00:00:54.618 --> 00:00:56.290
- Thank you.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.090
Well, just like you,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.938
I'm a mom of three

00:00:59.938 --> 00:01:03.860
and my young adults are
spread out in the Midwest.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:08.410
I wanna know how you balance
this fantastic career

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.610
plus your most important role

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.100
being a mom to Frankie and Olive.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.760
- You know, that's the most
important question, honestly.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.030
And the truth is, is that

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:22.790
I always sort of have an internal clock

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.310
where I know

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.480
that it's just--

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.950
it's been too much work

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.620
and I gotta get back to the kids.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.560
And we all feel like
when we're with our kids,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.310
that we're dropping balls at work.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.150
This is a natural seesaw

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.000
of parenthood and professional life.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.230
But my kids come first

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.770
and it's how I live my life,

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.500
and I'm very disciplined about
it, but I'll tell you this.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.090
It never feels like
I'm pulling it all off.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.540
So anyone else who beats
themselves up there,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.770
let's try to change that.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.380
Cause I am fault--

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.760
I am at fault of that too.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.329
Thank you Crystal, for your question.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:56.961
We wanna thank you.

00:01:56.961 --> 00:01:57.794
(audience claps)

00:01:57.794 --> 00:01:59.930
And if you wanna be one
of our virtual friends

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.320
come see us and get (claps)
your tickets right now

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.993
at the Drewbarrymoreshow.com.

00:02:04.993 --> 00:02:07.576
(upbeat music)

